[STEP 1] Recruitment
Group 1 -  Initial Assessment Team (IAT)
 Member 1 (Medical Oncologist (Lead)): Specializes in treating pancreatic adenocarcinoma; orchestrates treatment plans based on the responses observed in the phase 3 trial and assesses the overall efficacy of the novel chemotherapy agent.
 Member 2 (Clinical Pharmacologist): Provides expertise on drug pharmacodynamics and pharmacokinetics; reviews the dose
 Member 3 (Biostatistician): Analyzes data from the clinical trial; interprets the clinical significance of the outcomes and adverse events to provide statistical insight into the potential therapeutic index.

Group 2 -  Safety and Tolerability Team (STT)
 Member 1 (Clinical Toxicologist (Lead)): Reviews the adverse event data associated with different doses of the new chemotherapeutic agent; assesses the safety profile and implications for further dosing in clinical practice.
 Member 2 (Nurse Clinical Research Coordinator): Monitors adverse events during the study and collects patient
 Member 3 (Safety Pharmacologist): Evaluates the safety data and assists in identifying the severity, frequency, and types of treatment

Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Medical Oncologist (Lead)): Acts as the final authority; synthesizes inputs from IAT and STT to conclude the overall potential and safety of the novel treatment based on the therapeutic index calculations.
 Member 2 (Regulatory Affairs Specialist): Advises on FDA approval processes and requirements by providing a thorough understanding of the regulatory expectations based on the trial data and therapeutic index findings.
 Member 3 (Health Outcomes Researcher): Examines the implications of treatment decisions based on the therapeutic index; helps in strategizing how the results may influence future clinical practice and patient management.


